  "id": "COMPOUND:4107 - PROTEIN:801",
  "verbalization": "Arecoline is implicated in the interaction with the GABA(A) Receptor Benzodiazepine Binding Site through a chain of targets that ultimately converge on this receptor. The evidence suggests that Arecoline acts as a target for multiple 5-hydroxytryptamine receptors, including 5-HT2B, which in turn are targets of 2-Butan-2-Yl-3-Methoxypyrazine. This compound is also linked to the GABA(A) Receptor Benzodiazepine Binding Site, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of GABAergic signaling. The presence of multiple pathways converging on this receptor highlights a possible role in the pharmacological effects of Arecoline, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways underscores the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the importance of further investigation into the molecular interactions that govern this connection.",
